WHAT THIS PLUGIN IS, for anyone reading the licence before the README.

It is a set of instructions and reference material for an AI coding agent. It
contains no compiled software and no runtime. It reads Licentry's published
documentation over HTTPS, reads the repository it is pointed at, and writes
integration code into that repository.

It sends nothing to Licentry beyond ordinary requests for public documentation
pages. The source it reads goes to whichever AI provider the agent running it
already uses, under whatever agreement the operator has with that provider.
Licentry is not a party to that and receives none of it.

Code this plugin writes into a product carries a separate, perpetual licence
described in section 8 of the Licentry terms of service at
https://licentry.cc/terms. That licence does not expire with a subscription,
deliberately, because generated code ships inside binaries that outlive it.

Installing this plugin does not create a Licentry account and does not grant
access to anything behind a sign in, including the hardening guide it points
at, which stays tied to a vendor account.
